      "description": "<p>Latin America correspondent <strong>Tom Phillips </strong>reports on this Sunday’s historic presidential elections in Brazil, as the son of jailed former president Jair Bolsonaro hopes to take power</p><p>You would have been forgiven for thinking that when Jair Bolsonaro was convicted in September 2025 of attempting a coup, his political career was finished and his legacy forever tainted.</p><p>But in the first round of Brazil’s presidential elections this Sunday, another Bolsonaro has genuine hopes of victory – not Jair, but his son Flávio, who ialso campaigning to have his father released released.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2026/oct/02/the-bolsonarostheyre-back-brazil-heads-to-the-polls-podcast\">Continue reading...</a>",
